```
V → id      { V.code := give-name(id); V.type := give-type(id) }
V → ( E )   { V.code := E.code; V.type := E.type }
LHS → id    { LHS.code := give-name(id); LHS.type := give-type(id) }
```
(The question lists `give-type`/`give-name` after "name and type" — the functions obviously return type and name as their names say.)

```
T → T1 * V  { T.type := if T1.type = i and V.type = i then i else r;
              T.code := T1.code || V.code || '(*,' || T.type || ')' }
T → V       { T.code := V.code; T.type := V.type }
E → E1 + T  { E.type := if E1.type = i and T.type = i then i else r;
              E.code := E1.code || T.code || '(+,' || E.type || ')' }
E → T       { E.code := T.code; E.type := T.type }
```
